confidence in the court has collapsed. This is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:52.720
period that started with Trump and Republicans&nbsp;
putting in that six three conservative majority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:01:00.480
with the replacement of Ruth Bader Ginsburg by Amy&nbsp;
Coney Barrett. And that this has culminated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:06.320
the leak of the draft signaling that Roe v Wade&nbsp;
will be overturned. The last time Yahoo! YouGov&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.880
asked about confidence in the court with September&nbsp;
of 2020. That was just a few days after Ruth Bader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:18.240
Ginsburg died. Then 70% of registered voters said&nbsp;
they had some or a lot of confidence in the court,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:29.440
whereas 30% said they had a little or none. In the&nbsp;
new survey, a 40 point swing where now only half&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:36.800
